Hi Everybody,

I have a pair of AS4100 v4.0F clusters which has already been decommissioned 
some years ago however the business decided to re-activate this cluster for 
testing purposes. The situation is that this cluster setup contains the 
exact configuration as our newer ES40 4.0F clusters which had replaced the 
AS4100s. I need to provide a new set of hostname and IP addresses to both 
servers and the cluster alias to prevent any network conflicts with our 
production cluster.

So far I've started the servers in single-user mode to prevent ASE from 
starting. I have also already modified the hostnames and IP addresses of the 
AS4100s but I'm a little lost on how to go about modifying my cluster alias 
IP and hostname.

Given that both clusters share the exact cluster alias identities, how do I 
modify the AS4100 cluster alias hostname and IP address without starting ASE 
and without reconfiguring ASE from scratch? I'm guessing I'll need to hack 
into the /var/ase/config/asecdb to modify the cluster alias configuration 
but what utility can edit this file without starting ASE itself?

Any help will be much appreciated.

Regards,
Bobby

